MARS DB INGESTION
=================

This file documents the local learning database added by db.cpp.

Ethereum chain data
-------------------

The Ethereum path is intentionally direct: MARS talks to an Ethereum execution
JSON-RPC endpoint and calls eth_getBlockByNumber with full transaction objects.
Run your own node if possible. A hosted RPC endpoint works for small backfills,
but large historical ingestion will be rate-limited by most providers.

Environment:

    export ETH_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545

Initialize:

    ./mars db-init market.db

Backfill an explicit range:

    ./mars eth-update market.db 19000000 19001000

Resume from the last stored block and update to the current head:

    ./mars eth-update market.db 0 latest

Store only block-level aggregates, not every transaction:

    ./mars eth-update market.db 0 latest --blocks-only

Export block-level learning features:

    ./mars eth-export market.db eth_blocks.csv

The Ethereum tables are:

    eth_blocks
    eth_txs
    eth_block_features

FRED data
---------

Environment:

    export FRED_API_KEY=...

Update a macro panel:

    ./mars fred-update market.db DGS2,DGS10,T10Y2Y,VIXCLS,DTWEXBGS,WALCL

Export observations:

    ./mars fred-export market.db fred.csv

The FRED tables are:

    fred_series
    fred_observations

Design notes
------------

The database uses SQLite WAL mode, because the intended workflow is append-heavy
updates followed by read-heavy feature extraction. Ethereum JSON-RPC quantities
are stored in their original hex/string form where overflow or precision matters,
with approximate REAL columns added only for learning features.

This patch does not pretend chain variables are prices. eth-export emits chain
state features; they should later be joined to ETH market prices by timestamp for
training.
